From 306459130c79f6a2eb22faba6898a4d086ed908b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael A Cassaniti <michael@cassaniti.id.au>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 14:43:43 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Drivers/OptionRomPkg: Increase FTDI_TIMEOUT for
 virtualization

FTDI_TIMEOUT is set to 16ms, matching the hardware latency timer of
physical FTDI chips. Under virtualization (e.g. QEMU) or high system
load, host scheduling latency and burst console writes can easily
exceed 16ms, causing synchronous bulk transfers in WriteSerialIo to
time out prematurely and drop characters.

Increase FTDI_TIMEOUT from 16ms to 50ms (3x the hardware latency timer).
This provides sufficient margin for hypervisor scheduling jitter while
keeping worst-case blocking latency negligible if the device becomes
unresponsive.

Signed-off-by: Michael A Cassaniti <michael@cassaniti.id.au>
---
 .../OptionRomPkg/Bus/Usb/FtdiUsbSerialDxe/FtdiUsbSerialDriver.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Drivers/OptionRomPkg/Bus/Usb/FtdiUsbSerialDxe/FtdiUsbSerialDriver.h b/Drivers/OptionRomPkg/Bus/Usb/FtdiUsbSerialDxe/FtdiUsbSerialDriver.h
index 6048923..4f6699e 100644
--- a/Drivers/OptionRomPkg/Bus/Usb/FtdiUsbSerialDxe/FtdiUsbSerialDriver.h
+++ b/Drivers/OptionRomPkg/Bus/Usb/FtdiUsbSerialDxe/FtdiUsbSerialDriver.h
@@ -154,7 +154,7 @@ SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause-Patent
 //
 // FTDI timeout
 //
-#define FTDI_TIMEOUT       16
+#define FTDI_TIMEOUT       50
 
 //
 // FTDI FIFO depth
